# =========================================================================
# The PCB rev A2 build target.
#
#   idf.py -B build_pcb_a2 -DSDKCONFIG=build_pcb_a2/sdkconfig \
#          -DSDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS="sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.pcb_a2" build
#
# -DSDKCONFIG is not optional. `idf.py -B <dir>` gives
# the variant its own BUILD directory but NOT its own sdkconfig: that still
# defaults to <project>/sdkconfig, which the DevKit build also uses. So the
# first PCB build wrote CONFIG_SENTRY_BOARD_PCB_A2=y into the shared file, and
# every subsequent plain `idf.py build` silently produced a PCB image while
# calling itself the DevKit build. It was caught by a DIRAM figure that would
# not move when a guard that should have removed 2.3 KB was added - the
# measurement disagreed with the code, and the code was right.
#
# It is the exact failure this brief is about: two targets, one truth, and the
# one thing that must never happen is the wrong one being built silently. The
# defence is three-deep now. This flag, so the files cannot be shared; the
# `board=` line `I` prints, so a running device says which it is; and the
# no-regression certificate, which reads the board name back out of the built
# image and records it.
#
# Layered on top of sdkconfig.defaults, never instead of it, and built into
# its OWN directory - the sdkconfig.psram precedent, for the same reason. The
# DevKit target must keep producing exactly what `idf.py build` has always
# produced, and it cannot do that if a second target shares its build tree.
#
# THIS FILE SELECTS ONE THING: which header main/board_pins.h dispatches to.
# It sets no detector constant, no threshold, no tier default and no frame
# budget. Everything else - QIO, the partition table, 240 MHz, the float
# semantics, PSRAM off - comes from sdkconfig.defaults, which is FROZEN and
# is not edited here.
#
# Every hardware acceptance for this target is owed: it compiles, and that is
# the whole of the evidence.
# =========================================================================
CONFIG_SENTRY_BOARD_DEVKIT=n
CONFIG_SENTRY_BOARD_PCB_A2=y
